narrative:
## Your Weekly Planner

Programs can make decisions based on any type of data — including strings. Let's build a planner that gives advice depending on the day of the week.

### The Day Planner

```xiom
fn main() {
  let day: Str = "Friday";

  io.println("Today is: ");
  io.println(day);

  if day == "Monday" {
    io.println("Start the week strong — make a plan!");
  } elif day == "Tuesday" {
    io.println("Keep the momentum going — tackle a big task.");
  } elif day == "Wednesday" {
    io.println("Halfway there! Treat yourself to something nice.");
  } elif day == "Thursday" {
    io.println("Almost done — finish what you started.");
  } elif day == "Friday" {
    io.println("Last push! The weekend is almost here.");
  } elif day == "Saturday" {
    io.println("Relax and recharge — you earned it!");
  } elif day == "Sunday" {
    io.println("Get ready for the week ahead — plan tomorrow.");
  } else {
    io.println("That's not a day of the week!");
  }
}
```

Change the `day` variable and see how the output changes. The `else` at the end catches anything that isn't a valid day — a nice safety net!

